  "7516743829182517249": {
   "created": 1792131383,
   "author": "Anand A. Kekre",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aakekre_aiinfrastructure-inference-kvcache-activity-7516743829182517249-63R8",
   "text": "Everyone is watching CoreWeave\u2019s stock. I am watching the economics of inference.\n\nCoreWeave\u2019s stock has fallen sharply this week, while its bonds and credit-default swaps are signaling growing investor concerns about AI infrastructure debt.\n\nThe question isn\u2019t whether AI demand exists. It\u2019s whether the economics of GPU infrastructure can sustainably support the billions being invested.\n\nThe neocloud playbook has been straightforward:\u00a0raise billions in venture capital and debt financing, acquire GPUs, rent out compute, and maximize utilization. With enormous amounts of capital flowing into AI infrastructure, access to GPUs became a competitive advantage in itself. \n\nBut capital alone cannot ",
   "disc_score": 5,
